  "id": "COMPOUND:41386 - PROTEIN:5829",
  "verbalization": "Rubiyunnanin F is implicated in the target pathway leading to CHP-134 through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that Rubiyunnanin F acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by another compound, (2-Methyl-5-Prop-1-En-2-Ylcyclohex-2-En-1-Yl) Acetate. This compound, in turn, has a target of CHP-134. Additionally, Rubiyunnanin F is also linked to MIP, which is targeted by a complex molecule that also leads to CHP-134. These pathways collectively indicate that Rubiyunnanin F may influence CHP-134 through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving enzyme or receptor modulation. The integration of these evidence points suggests a potential role for Rubiyunnanin F in modulating CHP-134 via a complex network of targets, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
